    "name": "Hypertension Study (V4): Delayed vs Timely Diagnosis (G4 vs G1)",
    "description": "Primary causal contrast: delayed-diagnosis (G4, >12mo from first elevated BP) vs timely-diagnosis (G1, <=3mo), both incident-HTN treatment-naive (recording-comparable by construction). Time-at-risk anchored from the diagnosis date (cohort_start of the diagnosis-anchored strata) to avoid immortal-time bias. Cox PH, 1:1 PS matching. Empirically calibrated against 8 HTN-unrelated negative controls.",
